          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Years and Death</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Conrad continued to write but never achieved great financial success during his lifetime. His health declined, and he suffered from gout, which made writing difficult. Conrad died of a heart attack in 1924 in England, leaving behind a legacy as one of the greatest novelists in the English language.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Conrad's Legacy</strong><br>\nConrad's legacy is profound, influencing many writers with his narrative techniques and his themes of betrayal, isolation, and the clash between civilization and savagery. His use of a non-linear narrative and deep psychological insight were ahead of their time and remain subjects of academic study and literary acclaim.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Modern Literature</strong><br>\nConrad's impact on modern literature can be seen in the works of many authors who followed him. His narrative style and treatment of complex themes have earned him a place as a forerunner of modernist literature. Even today, his works continue to be read and appreciated for their intense moral scrutiny and narrative depth.</p>\n"
              },
